<title>USA: Mrs. Clinton returns from two-week Africa tour.</title>
<headline>Mrs. Clinton returns from two-week Africa tour.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hillary Rodham Clinton and daughter Chelsea returned home at sunrise on Sunday from a two-week tour of six African nations in time to celebrate Easter with President Bill Clinton.</p>
<p>Mrs. Clinton had flown overnight from Asmara, Eritrea in East Africa, last stop on a trip that also took her to Senegal, South Africa, Zimbabwe, Tanzania and Uganda.</p>
<p>The first lady's aides compiled a list of the total mileage of the trip and decided that Mrs. Clinton had travelled 19,291 miles (31,045 km).</p>
<p>There were also 500 miles (800 km) of motorcades, 24 miles (38 km) spent on boats, and 100 miles (160 km) on safari sightseeing tours.</p>
